WEBVTT

00:00:26.038 --> 00:00:31.413
Being 75% water,
they are swimmingly similar to fish.

00:00:31.454 --> 00:00:36.579
But their water composition drops to 65%
by their first birthday.

00:00:36.621 --> 00:00:39.121
So what role does water
play in our bodies,

00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:43.162
and how much do we actually 
need to drink to stay healthy?

00:00:43.204 --> 00:00:47.246
The H20 in our bodies works 
to cushion and lubricate joints,

00:00:47.287 --> 00:00:48.829
regulate temperature,

00:00:48.871 --> 00:00:52.537
and to nourish the brain and spinal cord.

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:55.246
Water isn't only in our blood.

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:59.662
An adult's brain and heart are almost
three quarters water.

00:00:59.704 --> 00:01:02.704
That's roughly equivalent to the amount
of moisture in a banana.